infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Install cost: compile from source vs ship prebuilds
  desc node-gyp compiles on every install machine; prebuilds ship the binary so install just copies the right one
  compares
    - label Compile at install (node-gyp)
      children
        - label Needs Python and a C/C++ compiler
          desc node-gyp wants Python, plus GCC/Clang (or MSVC on Windows)
        - label Needs Node headers for the running version
          desc Built against the exact Node version you run
        - label Reads binding.gyp, builds from source
          desc Generates a Makefile/Xcode/MSVC project and invokes the host compiler
        - label Breaks on minimal Docker, Alpine musl, Windows
          desc No toolchain on the box and install explodes with gyp ERR!
        - label Minutes of compile on every install
          desc npm install turns into building a C++ project
    - label Ship prebuilds (prebuildify)
      children
        - label No compiler, no Python at install
          desc Install just selects the matching prebuilt binary
        - label Binaries bundled in the npm tarball
          desc Zero network, zero compile, fully offline installs
        - label Node-API: one prebuild per platform
          desc An ABI-stable binary serves every Node version
        - label Matrix shrinks to platforms only
          desc One per platform, not one per platform per Node version
        - label Build cost moves to your CI pipeline
          desc You still build once per platform/arch/libc you support
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
